# The opt-in Bayes lock (requirements/README.md "Extras"; ./install.sh --with-bayes, docs/BAYES.md §2.9): the
# tools venv plus what hooks/stack_bayes.py, the detached fitter, imports. Compiled with the tools command and
# -c requirements/tools.txt, so every package the two locks share has the same pin. Pins: the prototype's lock
# (docs/bayes/b1v2/fit_prototype.py.lock, also WP2's fit), re-checked at lock time (2026-10-09): pytensor is
# 3.3.2, not the prototype's 3.3.3, which was published 2026-10-02T14:13Z, inside the 7-day cooldown (pymc
# 6.3.2 asks pytensor>=3.2.2,<3.4); re-lock to 3.3.3 on or after 2026-10-10. Without this lock
# stack_usage.bayes_fit records skipped:no-pymc.
-r tools.in
pymc==6.3.2                 # hooks/stack_bayes.py
pytensor==3.3.2             # hooks/stack_bayes.py
nutpie==0.16.11             # hooks/stack_bayes.py (pm.sample nuts_sampler="nutpie")
arviz==1.3.0                # hooks/stack_bayes.py
scipy==1.18.1               # hooks/stack_bayes.py
